  "responseTimeMs": 17326,
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nPenalties for late filing of a VAT return include a fine of PHP 1,000 and an additional 25% of the tax due, as specified under the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe relevant provisions are found in the NIRC, specifically:\n- **Section 248**: Imposes penalties for failure to file returns and pay taxes.\n- **Section 249**: Details the penalties for late payment of taxes.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor businesses, this means that failing to file VAT returns on time can lead to significant financial penalties. It is crucial for VAT-registered entities to maintain accurate records and ensure timely submissions to avoid these penalties, which can accumulate and impact cash flow. Regular reminders and compliance checks can help mitigate the risk of incurring these penalties.",
